{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-69253","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100128","text":"κ Integration Spec: Product-Level Specification"}]},{"id":"blk-69254","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100129","text":"Version 0.2.0 — Normalized"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100130","text":"How the cyclicity invariant κ is computed, surfaced, and used across Graphonomous, BendScript, Deliberatic, TickTickClock, and the [&] Protocol.  "},{"id":"spn-100131","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.2.0 changes (from Codex review):"},{"id":"spn-100132","text":" - Normalized all field names to a single canonical schema (§2.4) - Resolved tool naming: "},{"id":"spn-100133","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_topology"},{"id":"spn-100134","text":" is the standalone tool; "},{"id":"spn-100135","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-100136","text":" gains a "},{"id":"spn-100137","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-100138","text":" field — no "},{"id":"spn-100139","marks":["code"],"text":"memory_recall_with_topology"},{"id":"spn-100140","text":" tool - Fixed approximation representation: "},{"id":"spn-100141","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-100142","text":" is always an integer; large SCCs add "},{"id":"spn-100143","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-100144","text":" (no "},{"id":"spn-100145","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-100146","text":" field) - Added instrumentation requirements (§7) - Clarified BendScript directed-edge policy (§4.3)"}]}],"id":"blk-69255","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-69257","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100147","text":"1. Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-69258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100148","text":"κ (kappa) is a graph-theoretic invariant that measures the minimum irreducible bidirectional information flow in a directed graph. It is the routing primitive that determines whether a query region of a knowledge graph requires single-pass retrieval (κ = 0) or iterative deliberation (κ > 0)."}]},{"id":"blk-69259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100149","text":"This spec defines:"}]},{"id":"blk-69260","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69262","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100150","text":"How κ is computed"}]}],"id":"blk-69261","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100151","text":"Where it is computed in the stack"}]}],"id":"blk-69263","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100152","text":"How it routes inference"}]}],"id":"blk-69265","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100153","text":"How it is surfaced to users"}]}],"id":"blk-69267","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100154","text":"How it integrates with each product"}]}],"id":"blk-69269","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69271","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100155","text":"2. Computation"}]},{"id":"blk-69272","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100156","text":"2.1 Algorithm"}]},{"id":"blk-69273","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function compute_kappa(graph):\n    # Pre-step: define node universe U from the analyzed subgraph/query result.\n    # Ignore any edge where src ∉ U or dst ∉ U.\n    # Exclude self-loops (u -> u) from adjacency for κ computation.\n    # Step 1: Find all strongly connected components\n    sccs = tarjan_scc(graph)                    # O(V + E)\n\n    # Step 2: For each nontrivial SCC (size > 1)\n    results = []\n    for scc in sccs where |scc| > 1:\n        # Step 3: Enumerate bipartitions, find minimum bidirectional cut\n        k = infinity\n        for (A, B) in nontrivial_bipartitions(scc):\n            edges_a_to_b = count_edges(A, B, graph)\n            edges_b_to_a = count_edges(B, A, graph)\n            bidirectional_cut = min(edges_a_to_b, edges_b_to_a)\n            k = min(k, bidirectional_cut)\n            if k == 0: break  # early exit (can't go lower)\n\n        # Step 4: Record SCC with its κ value and minimum-cut partition\n        results.append({\n            scc: scc,\n            kappa: k,\n            min_cut_partition: (A_min, B_min),\n            min_cut_edges: edges_achieving_minimum\n        })\n\n    return results"},{"id":"blk-69274","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100157","text":"2.2 Complexity"}]},{"id":"blk-69275","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69277","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100158","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC decomposition:"},{"id":"spn-100159","text":" O(V + E) via Tarjan's algorithm"}]}],"id":"blk-69276","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100160","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ computation per SCC:"},{"id":"spn-100161","text":" O(2^|SCC| × |SCC|²) in the worst case (enumerating all bipartitions)"}]}],"id":"blk-69278","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Practical constraint:"},{"id":"spn-100163","text":" For SCCs up to ~20 nodes, bipartition enumeration is feasible in real time. For larger SCCs, use approximation:"}]}],"id":"blk-69280","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100164","text":"Return SCC size as a proxy for κ, with "},{"id":"spn-100165","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-100166","text":" flag"}]}],"id":"blk-69282","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100167","text":"κ field remains an integer (the estimate), never a symbol/atom/string"}]}],"id":"blk-69284","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100168","marks":["bold"],"text":"Node-universe rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-100169","text":" Analyze only the node set supplied by retrieval/query scope (or explicit "},{"id":"spn-100170","marks":["code"],"text":"node_ids"},{"id":"spn-100171","text":" input). Do not pull in external nodes implicitly during κ analysis."}]}],"id":"blk-69286","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100172","marks":["bold"],"text":"Self-loop rule (NORMATIVE):"},{"id":"spn-100173","text":" Exclude self-loops ("},{"id":"spn-100174","marks":["code"],"text":"source == target"},{"id":"spn-100175","text":") from κ adjacency and cut counts."}]}],"id":"blk-69288","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69290","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100176","text":"2.3 Incremental Updates"}]},{"id":"blk-69291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100177","text":"When an edge is added or removed from the knowledge graph:"}]},{"id":"blk-69292","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100178","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge addition:"},{"id":"spn-100179","text":" Can only merge SCCs or enlarge existing ones. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. If a new nontrivial SCC is formed, compute κ for it."}]}],"id":"blk-69293","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100180","marks":["bold"],"text":"Edge removal:"},{"id":"spn-100181","text":" Can only split SCCs or shrink them. Re-run Tarjan on the affected component. Recompute κ for any remaining nontrivial SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-69295","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100182","marks":["bold"],"text":"Optimization:"},{"id":"spn-100183","text":" Maintain an SCC index alongside the knowledge graph. Incremental SCC algorithms (e.g., Bender, Fineman & Gilbert 2015) can update SCCs in O(V) amortized per edge change."}]}],"id":"blk-69297","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-69299","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100184","text":"2.4 Canonical Schema (NORMATIVE — all implementations must match)"}]},{"id":"blk-69300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100185","text":"Every κ topology result — whether from Elixir, JavaScript, or MCP JSON — uses these exact field names:"}]},{"id":"blk-69301","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"sccs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n      \"nodes\": [\"node-a\", \"node-b\"],\n      \"kappa\": 2,\n      \"approximate\": false,\n      \"fault_line_edges\": [\n        {\"source\": \"node-a\", \"target\": \"node-b\"}\n      ],\n      \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"deliberation_budget\": {\n        \"max_iterations\": 3,\n        \"agent_count\": 2,\n        \"timeout_multiplier\": 2.0,\n        \"confidence_threshold\": 0.80\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dag_nodes\": [\"node-x\", \"node-y\"],\n  \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n  \"max_kappa\": 2,\n  \"scc_count\": 1\n}"},{"id":"blk-69302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100186","marks":["bold"],"text":"Field name rules (resolves all drift):"}]},{"id":"blk-69303","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100187","text":"Top-level routing key: "},{"id":"spn-100188","marks":["code"],"text":"routing"},{"id":"spn-100189","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-100190","marks":["code"],"text":"overall_routing"},{"id":"spn-100191","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-69304","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100192","text":"Edge endpoints: "},{"id":"spn-100193","marks":["code"],"text":"source"},{"id":"spn-100194","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-100195","marks":["code"],"text":"target"},{"id":"spn-100196","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-100197","marks":["code"],"text":"from"},{"id":"spn-100198","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-100199","marks":["code"],"text":"to"},{"id":"spn-100200","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-100201","marks":["code"],"text":"a"},{"id":"spn-100202","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-100203","marks":["code"],"text":"b"},{"id":"spn-100204","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-69306","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100205","text":"Fault lines: "},{"id":"spn-100206","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-100207","text":" (not "},{"id":"spn-100208","marks":["code"],"text":"min_cut_edges"},{"id":"spn-100209","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-69308","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100210","text":"κ type: always "},{"id":"spn-100211","marks":["code"],"text":"integer"},{"id":"spn-100212","text":" (never string, atom, or symbol)"}]}],"id":"blk-69310","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100213","text":"Approximation: "},{"id":"spn-100214","marks":["code"],"text":"\"approximate\": true"},{"id":"spn-100215","text":" boolean flag on the SCC object; "},{"id":"spn-100216","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-100217","text":" still holds the integer estimate"}]}],"id":"blk-69312","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100218","text":"Routing values: "},{"id":"spn-100219","marks":["code"],"text":"\"fast\""},{"id":"spn-100220","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-100221","marks":["code"],"text":"\"deliberate\""},{"id":"spn-100222","text":" (strings in JSON, atoms "},{"id":"spn-100223","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-100224","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-100225","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-100226","text":" in Elixir, strings in JS)"}]}],"id":"blk-69314","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100227","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema boundary rules (NORMATIVE):"}]},{"id":"blk-69317","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69319","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100228","marks":["bold"],"text":"On MCP/JSON boundaries:"},{"id":"spn-100229","text":" use canonical snake_case keys exactly as defined in §2.4 ("},{"id":"spn-100230","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-100231","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100232","marks":["code"],"text":"max_kappa"},{"id":"spn-100233","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100234","marks":["code"],"text":"scc_count"},{"id":"spn-100235","text":", etc.)."}]}],"id":"blk-69318","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69321","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100236","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside Elixir runtime:"},{"id":"spn-100237","text":" atoms are allowed for routing values ("},{"id":"spn-100238","marks":["code"],"text":":fast"},{"id":"spn-100239","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100240","marks":["code"],"text":":deliberate"},{"id":"spn-100241","text":"), but keys remain canonical and are serialized to JSON strings at the boundary."}]}],"id":"blk-69320","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69323","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100242","marks":["bold"],"text":"Inside JavaScript UI code:"},{"id":"spn-100243","text":" camelCase mirrors are allowed for local-only objects ("},{"id":"spn-100244","marks":["code"],"text":"faultLineEdges"},{"id":"spn-100245","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100246","marks":["code"],"text":"maxKappa"},{"id":"spn-100247","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100248","marks":["code"],"text":"sccCount"},{"id":"spn-100249","text":") for ergonomics, but any network payload or persisted topology record must be converted back to canonical snake_case."}]}],"id":"blk-69322","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100250","marks":["bold"],"text":"Elixir atom mapping:"}]},{"id":"blk-69325","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Elixir uses atoms internally, converts to strings for MCP JSON\n:fast       → \"fast\"\n:deliberate → \"deliberate\""},{"id":"blk-69326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100251","marks":["bold"],"text":"JavaScript mapping (local only):"}]},{"id":"blk-69327","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"// Local object ergonomics\n{ faultLineEdges, maxKappa, sccCount, routing }\n\n// MCP / wire payloads must remain canonical snake_case\n{ fault_line_edges, max_kappa, scc_count, routing }"},{"id":"blk-69328","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100252","text":"3. Routing Logic"}]},{"id":"blk-69329","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100253","text":"3.1 The κ Router"}]},{"id":"blk-69330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100254","text":"The κ router sits between memory retrieval and reasoning. It inspects the topological structure of the retrieved subgraph and makes a routing decision."}]},{"id":"blk-69331","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function kappa_route(retrieved_subgraph):\n    scc_analysis = compute_kappa(retrieved_subgraph)\n\n    dag_context = nodes NOT in any nontrivial SCC\n    scc_contexts = scc_analysis  # list of {scc, kappa, fault_line_edges, ...}\n\n    # DAG regions: single-pass retrieval\n    retrieval_context = topological_sort_and_collect(dag_context)\n\n    # SCC regions: flag for deliberation\n    deliberation_tasks = []\n    for scc_info in scc_contexts:\n        deliberation_tasks.append({\n            nodes: scc_info.scc,\n            kappa: scc_info.kappa,\n            fault_lines: scc_info.fault_line_edges,\n            budget: deliberation_budget(scc_info.kappa)\n        })\n\n    return {\n        retrieval_context: retrieval_context,\n        deliberation_tasks: deliberation_tasks,\n        routing: \"fast\" if len(deliberation_tasks) == 0 else \"deliberate\"\n    }"},{"id":"blk-69332","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100255","text":"3.2 Deliberation Budget Function"}]},{"id":"blk-69333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100256","text":"The deliberation budget maps κ to concrete inference parameters. This is an engineering heuristic (not proved — to be tuned empirically). Caps on "},{"id":"spn-100257","marks":["code"],"text":"max_iterations"},{"id":"spn-100258","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-100259","marks":["code"],"text":"confidence_threshold"},{"id":"spn-100260","text":" are required to prevent runaway values when "},{"id":"spn-100261","marks":["code"],"text":"approximate: true"},{"id":"spn-100262","text":" SCCs use size-based κ estimates:"}]},{"id":"blk-69334","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"function deliberation_budget(kappa):\n    return {\n        max_iterations: min(kappa + 1, 4),\n        agent_count: min(kappa, 3),\n        timeout_multiplier: min(1.0 + 0.5*kappa, 3.5),\n        confidence_threshold: min(0.7 + 0.05*kappa, 0.95)\n    }"},{"id":"blk-69335","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100263","text":"3.3 The Fast Path vs. Deliberation Path"}]},{"id":"blk-69336","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  Query arrives   │\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  &memory.recall  │   Graphonomous retrieves relevant subgraph\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n                      ▼\n             ┌─────────────────┐\n             │  κ Router        │   Compute SCCs, κ values\n             └────────┬────────┘\n                      │\n              ┌───────┴────────┐\n              │                │\n         κ = 0 (all DAG)    κ > 0 (has SCCs)\n              │                │\n              ▼                ▼\n       ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n       │ Fast Path │    │  Deliberation │\n       │ single    │    │  &reason via  │\n       │ pass      │    │  Deliberatic  │\n       │ retrieval │    │  κ-informed   │\n       └─────┬────┘    │  budget       │\n             │         └──────┬───────┘\n             │                │\n             └───────┬────────┘\n                     │\n                     ▼\n             ┌──────────────┐\n             │  &memory.learn │   Results feed back into graph\n             └──────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-69337","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100264","text":"4. Product Integration"}]},{"id":"blk-69338","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100265","text":"4.1 Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-69339","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100266","marks":["bold"],"text":"Where κ lives:"},{"id":"spn-100267","text":" Computed at query time on the retrieved subgraph. Cached per SCC in the knowledge graph index; invalidated on edge changes."}]},{"id":"blk-69340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100268","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-69341","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100269","marks":["code"],"text":"Retriever.retrieve/2"},{"id":"spn-100270","text":" now returns a "},{"id":"spn-100271","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-100272","text":" key alongside existing "},{"id":"spn-100273","marks":["code"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-100274","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100275","marks":["code"],"text":"causal_context"},{"id":"spn-100276","text":", "},{"id":"spn-100277","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"}]}],"id":"blk-69342","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100278","text":"New module "},{"id":"spn-100279","marks":["code"],"text":"Graphonomous.Topology"},{"id":"spn-100280","text":" computes and returns the full SCC analysis for a given subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-69344","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100281","text":"New function "},{"id":"spn-100282","marks":["code"],"text":"Store.list_edges_between/1"},{"id":"spn-100283","text":" fetches edges within a node set"}]}],"id":"blk-69346","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100284","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `analyze_topology` (NEW standalone tool):"}]},{"id":"blk-69349","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"analyze_topology\",\n  \"description\": \"Compute topological structure (SCCs, κ values, routing decision) for a set of nodes in the knowledge graph.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"node_ids\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n        \"description\": \"Node IDs to analyze. If omitted, analyzes the full graph.\"\n      },\n      \"query\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"Optional query text. If provided, retrieves relevant nodes first, then analyzes their topology.\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-69350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100285","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool: `retrieve_context` (EXISTING — augmented with topology):"}]},{"id":"blk-69351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100286","text":"The existing "},{"id":"spn-100287","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-100288","text":" tool gains a "},{"id":"spn-100289","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-100290","text":" field in its response. No new tool name — same endpoint, richer response:"}]},{"id":"blk-69352","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"query\": \"company strategy\",\n  \"count\": 7,\n  \"results\": [\"...existing results...\"],\n  \"causal_context\": [\"...existing...\"],\n  \"stats\": {\"...existing...\"},\n  \"topology\": {\n    \"sccs\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scc-0\",\n        \"nodes\": [\"market-share\", \"revenue\", \"r-and-d\", \"product-quality\", \"customer-retention\"],\n        \"kappa\": 1,\n        \"approximate\": false,\n        \"fault_line_edges\": [\n          {\"source\": \"product-quality\", \"target\": \"market-share\"}\n        ],\n        \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n        \"deliberation_budget\": {\n          \"max_iterations\": 2,\n          \"agent_count\": 1,\n          \"timeout_multiplier\": 1.5,\n          \"confidence_threshold\": 0.75\n        }\n      }\n    ],\n    \"dag_nodes\": [\"founding-date\", \"ceo-name\", \"headquarters\"],\n    \"routing\": \"deliberate\",\n    \"max_kappa\": 1,\n    \"scc_count\": 1\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-69353","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100291","text":"4.2 Deliberatic"}]},{"id":"blk-69354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100292","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-69355","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100293","text":"Accepts "},{"id":"spn-100294","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-100295","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-100296","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-100297","text":" as input parameters on its deliberation endpoint."}]}],"id":"blk-69356","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100298","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-100299","marks":["code"],"text":"kappa"},{"id":"spn-100300","text":" to set argumentation depth (number of rounds)."}]}],"id":"blk-69358","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100301","text":"Uses "},{"id":"spn-100302","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_line_edges"},{"id":"spn-100303","text":" (minimum-cut edges) to generate the initial propositions that agents must argue about — these are the critical bidirectional dependencies."}]}],"id":"blk-69360","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100304","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP tool additions:"}]},{"id":"blk-69363","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"name\": \"deliberate_on_scc\",\n  \"description\": \"Run structured argumentation on a strongly connected knowledge cluster. Uses κ to set deliberation budget and fault lines to seed propositions.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"scc_nodes\": { \"type\": \"array\", \"items\": { \"type\": \"string\" } },\n      \"scc_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"kappa\": { \"type\": \"integer\" },\n      \"fault_line_edges\": { \"type\": \"array\" },\n      \"governance\": { \"type\": \"object\" }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-69364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100305","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key insight:"},{"id":"spn-100306","text":" Deliberatic doesn't need to know about graph theory. It receives a set of propositions (derived from fault lines), a budget (derived from κ), and it argues. The graph intelligence lives in Graphonomous; the argumentation intelligence lives in Deliberatic. κ is the handshake between them."}]},{"id":"blk-69365","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100307","text":"4.3 BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-69366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100308","marks":["bold"],"text":"What changes:"}]},{"id":"blk-69367","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100309","text":"Directed-Edge Policy (NORMATIVE)"}]},{"id":"blk-69368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100310","text":"BendScript edges have a "},{"id":"spn-100311","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-100312","text":" property. For κ computation, edge directionality is determined by kind:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-69370","spans":[{"id":"spn-100313","text":"Edge kind"}]},{"id":"blk-69371","spans":[{"id":"spn-100314","text":"Directionality for κ"}]},{"id":"blk-69372","spans":[{"id":"spn-100315","text":"Rationale"}]}],"id":"blk-69369","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-69373","spans":[{"id":"spn-100316","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"}]},{"id":"blk-69374","spans":[{"id":"spn-100317","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-100318","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-69375","spans":[{"id":"spn-100319","text":"Cause precedes effect"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69376","spans":[{"id":"spn-100320","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"}]},{"id":"blk-69377","spans":[{"id":"spn-100321","marks":["bold"],"text":"Directed"},{"id":"spn-100322","text":" (a → b)"}]},{"id":"blk-69378","spans":[{"id":"spn-100323","text":"Before precedes after"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69379","spans":[{"id":"spn-100324","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-69380","spans":[{"id":"spn-100325","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-100326","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-69381","spans":[{"id":"spn-100327","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69382","spans":[{"id":"spn-100328","marks":["code"],"text":"associative"}]},{"id":"blk-69383","spans":[{"id":"spn-100329","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-100330","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-69384","spans":[{"id":"spn-100331","text":"Symmetric, no feedback"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69385","spans":[{"id":"spn-100332","marks":["code"],"text":"user"}]},{"id":"blk-69386","spans":[{"id":"spn-100333","marks":["bold"],"text":"Skip"},{"id":"spn-100334","text":" (excluded from κ graph)"}]},{"id":"blk-69387","spans":[{"id":"spn-100335","text":"Ambiguous directionality"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-69388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100336","text":"This is a "},{"id":"spn-100337","marks":["bold"],"text":"hard rule"},{"id":"spn-100338","text":", not a toggle. Only "},{"id":"spn-100339","marks":["code"],"text":"causal"},{"id":"spn-100340","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-100341","marks":["code"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-100342","text":" edges participate in SCC/κ computation. The filter constant:"}]},{"id":"blk-69389","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const DIRECTED_KINDS = ['causal', 'temporal'];"},{"id":"blk-69390","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100343","text":"Visual Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-69391","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100344","marks":["bold"],"text":"SCC clusters rendered visually:"},{"id":"spn-100345","text":" Nodes within a nontrivial SCC share a colored halo or background region. Color intensity scales with κ."}]}],"id":"blk-69392","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100346","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minimum-cut edges highlighted:"},{"id":"spn-100347","text":" Fault-line edges rendered in dashed style ("},{"id":"spn-100348","marks":["code"],"text":"ctx.setLineDash([6, 4])"},{"id":"spn-100349","text":") with brighter color."}]}],"id":"blk-69394","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100350","marks":["bold"],"text":"κ badge on SCC clusters:"},{"id":"spn-100351","text":" Each SCC cluster shows its κ value as a small badge, e.g., \"κ=2\"."}]}],"id":"blk-69396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69398","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100352","text":"Interaction Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-69399","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100353","marks":["bold"],"text":"Topology preview via context menu:"},{"id":"spn-100354","text":" When the user right-clicks a node and selects \"Connect to…\" (a new context menu item), BendScript shows candidate target nodes with topology impact annotations:"}]}],"id":"blk-69400","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100355","text":"\"→ NodeX: creates feedback loop (κ: 0→1)\""}]}],"id":"blk-69402","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100356","text":"\"→ NodeY: strengthens loop (κ: 1→2)\""}]}],"id":"blk-69404","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100357","text":"\"→ NodeZ: no topological change\""}]}],"id":"blk-69406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100358","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Bend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-100359","text":" Right-click context menu on DAG nodes — automatically suggests the nearest edge that would create a feedback loop."}]}],"id":"blk-69408","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100360","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Unbend\" action:"},{"id":"spn-100361","text":" Right-click context menu on SCC nodes — identifies the fault-line edge and offers to remove it."}]}],"id":"blk-69410","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100362","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note:"},{"id":"spn-100363","text":" BendScript does NOT currently have drag-to-connect edge creation. The topology preview is accessed via the context menu \"Connect to…\" flow. Do not implement drag-to-connect in this phase."}]},{"id":"blk-69413","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100364","text":"HUD"}]},{"id":"blk-69414","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100365","marks":["bold"],"text":"Global κ display:"},{"id":"spn-100366","text":" The existing HUD gains a κ readout showing the maximum κ across all SCCs in the graph, and a count of SCCs."}]}],"id":"blk-69415","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100367","marks":["bold"],"text":"Routing indicator:"},{"id":"spn-100368","text":" \"mode: RETRIEVAL\" (all κ = 0) or \"mode: DELIBERATION\" (any κ > 0)."}]}],"id":"blk-69417","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69419","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100369","text":"4.4 The [&] Protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-69420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100370","marks":["bold"],"text":"Grammar extension:"}]},{"id":"blk-69421","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"# Extended [&] capability grammar — topology-aware routing\nTopologyOp      := \"&topology\" \".\" (\"analyze\" | \"route\" | \"kappa\")\n\n# Updated pipeline pattern\nInferencePipeline :=\n    \"&memory.recall\" \"(\" QueryExpr \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.analyze\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&topology.route\" \"()\"\n    \"|>\" \"&reason.deliberate\" \"(\" \"budget:\" \":κ\" \")\"\n    \"|>\" \"&memory.learn\" \"()\""},{"id":"blk-69422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100371","marks":["bold"],"text":"Schema extension (ampersand.schema.json):"}]},{"id":"blk-69423","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&topology.analyze\": {\n      \"provider\": \"graphonomous\",\n      \"description\": \"Compute SCC decomposition and κ values for a subgraph\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"max_scc_size_for_exact\": 20,\n        \"approximation_strategy\": \"scc_size_proxy\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"&topology.route\": {\n      \"provider\": \"builtin\",\n      \"description\": \"Route inference based on κ: DAG regions → fast path, SCC regions → deliberation\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"deliberation_provider\": \"deliberatic\",\n        \"fast_path_provider\": \"graphonomous\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-69424","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100372","text":"4.5 TickTickClock"}]},{"id":"blk-69425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100373","marks":["bold"],"text":"Connection:"},{"id":"spn-100374","text":" For discrete time-series dynamics, the transition graph of the system has κ > 0 if and only if the system has a periodic orbit. TickTickClock can use this as a formal periodicity detector:"}]},{"id":"blk-69426","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69428","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100375","text":"Discretize time-series data into state transitions"}]}],"id":"blk-69427","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100376","text":"Build the transition graph"}]}],"id":"blk-69429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100377","text":"Compute κ"}]}],"id":"blk-69431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100378","text":"κ > 0 → periodic pattern detected, flag for temporal reasoning"}]}],"id":"blk-69433","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100379","text":"κ = 0 → pure drift, no recurrence"}]}],"id":"blk-69435","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100380","text":"This is a secondary integration (TickTickClock already has Mamba SSM for pattern detection), but it provides a complementary structural signal."}]},{"id":"blk-69438","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100381","text":"4.6 OpenSentience"}]},{"id":"blk-69439","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100382","marks":["bold"],"text":"Role:"},{"id":"spn-100383","text":" Research home for the theoretical foundations. Hosts:"}]},{"id":"blk-69440","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100384","text":"The κ paper (theoretical background, proofs, categorical framework)"}]}],"id":"blk-69441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100385","text":"The proof code (runnable verification)"}]}],"id":"blk-69443","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100386","text":"Interactive demos (live κ computation on user-constructed graphs)"}]}],"id":"blk-69445","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100387","text":"The original Scale Topology Axis essay (broader theoretical context connecting κ to physics, cosmology, and consciousness science)"}]}],"id":"blk-69447","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69449","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100388","text":"5. Implementation Priority"}]},{"id":"blk-69450","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100389","text":"Phase 1: Core (ship first)"}]},{"id":"blk-69451","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100390","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to Elixir (Graphonomous server-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-69452","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100391","text":"[ ] Port κ computation to JavaScript (BendScript client-side)"}]}],"id":"blk-69454","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69457","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100392","text":"[ ] Integrate Tarjan's SCC into Graphonomous's graph index"}]}],"id":"blk-69456","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100393","text":"[ ] Return topology annotations from "},{"id":"spn-100394","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]}],"id":"blk-69458","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100395","text":"[ ] Add SCC visualization to BendScript canvas"}]}],"id":"blk-69460","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69462","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100396","text":"Phase 2: Routing (ship second)"}]},{"id":"blk-69463","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100397","text":"[ ] Implement κ router in the [&] pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-69464","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100398","text":"[ ] Connect κ router to Deliberatic trigger"}]}],"id":"blk-69466","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100399","text":"[ ] Add deliberation budget function"}]}],"id":"blk-69468","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100400","text":"[ ] Test on real knowledge graph queries: does κ-aware routing improve answer quality?"}]}],"id":"blk-69470","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69472","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100401","text":"Phase 3: Polish (ship third)"}]},{"id":"blk-69473","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100402","text":"[ ] BendScript topology preview via context menu"}]}],"id":"blk-69474","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69477","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100403","text":"[ ] Bend/Unbend context menu actions"}]}],"id":"blk-69476","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100404","text":"[ ] HUD κ display and routing indicator"}]}],"id":"blk-69478","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100405","text":"[ ] TickTickClock periodicity detection via κ"}]}],"id":"blk-69480","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100406","text":"[ ] OpenSentience publication of κ paper and demos"}]}],"id":"blk-69482","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69484","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100407","text":"Phase 4: Optimization"}]},{"id":"blk-69485","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100408","text":"[ ] Incremental SCC maintenance (avoid full recomputation on every edge change)"}]}],"id":"blk-69486","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100409","text":"[ ] Approximate κ for large SCCs (> 20 nodes)"}]}],"id":"blk-69488","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69491","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100410","text":"[ ] Benchmark: latency impact of topology computation on query path"}]}],"id":"blk-69490","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69493","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100411","text":"[ ] A/B test: κ-routed inference vs. uniform retrieval on quality metrics"}]}],"id":"blk-69492","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69494","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100412","text":"6. Success Metrics"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-69496","spans":[{"id":"spn-100413","text":"Metric"}]},{"id":"blk-69497","spans":[{"id":"spn-100414","text":"Baseline (no κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-69498","spans":[{"id":"spn-100415","text":"Target (with κ)"}]},{"id":"blk-69499","spans":[{"id":"spn-100416","text":"How to Measure"}]}],"id":"blk-69495","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-69500","spans":[{"id":"spn-100417","text":"Answer coherence on circular topics"}]},{"id":"blk-69501","spans":[{"id":"spn-100418","text":"Human eval ~60%"}]},{"id":"blk-69502","spans":[{"id":"spn-100419","text":"Human eval ~80%"}]},{"id":"blk-69503","spans":[{"id":"spn-100420","text":"Blind eval on queries touching SCCs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69504","spans":[{"id":"spn-100421","text":"Unnecessary deliberation calls"}]},{"id":"blk-69505","spans":[{"id":"spn-100422","text":"N/A (no routing)"}]},{"id":"blk-69506","spans":[{"id":"spn-100423","text":"< 20% of queries"}]},{"id":"blk-69507","spans":[{"id":"spn-100424","text":"Track κ=0 queries that hit deliberation anyway"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69508","spans":[{"id":"spn-100425","text":"Deliberation convergence speed"}]},{"id":"blk-69509","spans":[{"id":"spn-100426","text":"Fixed rounds"}]},{"id":"blk-69510","spans":[{"id":"spn-100427","text":"κ+1 rounds avg"}]},{"id":"blk-69511","spans":[{"id":"spn-100428","text":"Measure rounds to convergence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69512","spans":[{"id":"spn-100429","text":"User engagement in BendScript"}]},{"id":"blk-69513","spans":[{"id":"spn-100430","text":"Nodes/edges per session"}]},{"id":"blk-69514","spans":[{"id":"spn-100431","text":"+30%"}]},{"id":"blk-69515","spans":[{"id":"spn-100432","text":"Track topology actions (bend/unbend/stargate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-69516","spans":[{"id":"spn-100433","text":"OpenSentience traffic"}]},{"id":"blk-69517","spans":[{"id":"spn-100434","text":"Baseline"}]},{"id":"blk-69518","spans":[{"id":"spn-100435","text":"Organic from dev community"}]},{"id":"blk-69519","spans":[{"id":"spn-100436","text":"Track referrals from product UIs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-69520","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100437","text":"7. Instrumentation Requirements (NEW in v0.2.0)"}]},{"id":"blk-69521","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100438","text":"All κ computation must emit telemetry. This is required for Gate C (performance) and Gate D (product effect) validation."}]},{"id":"blk-69522","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100439","text":"7.1 Latency Counters (Elixir — "},{"id":"spn-100440","marks":["code"],"text":":telemetry"},{"id":"spn-100441","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-69523","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Emit on every topology computation\n# REQUIRED UNIT: duration_ms (float milliseconds)\n# If measured via :timer.tc/1, convert with: duration_ms = duration_us / 1000.0\n:telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :analyze],\n  %{duration_ms: elapsed_ms, node_count: n, edge_count: e},\n  %{scc_count: scc_count, max_kappa: max_kappa, routing: routing}\n)"},{"id":"blk-69524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100442","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-69525","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100443","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.duration_ms"},{"id":"spn-100444","text":" — p50, p95, p99 (canonical latency metric)"}]}],"id":"blk-69526","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100445","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.node_count"},{"id":"spn-100446","text":" — distribution of subgraph sizes"}]}],"id":"blk-69528","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69531","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100447","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.edge_count"},{"id":"spn-100448","text":" — distribution of subgraph densities"}]}],"id":"blk-69530","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69533","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100449","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.scc_count"},{"id":"spn-100450","text":" — how often SCCs are found"}]}],"id":"blk-69532","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69535","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100451","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.routing.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-100452","text":" — deliberate / total analyzes"}]}],"id":"blk-69534","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69537","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100453","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.analyze.self_loop_filtered_count"},{"id":"spn-100454","text":" — number of self-loops ignored during adjacency construction"}]}],"id":"blk-69536","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69538","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100455","text":"7.2 Routing Decision Counters"}]},{"id":"blk-69539","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":":telemetry.execute(\n  [:graphonomous, :topology, :route],\n  %{},\n  %{decision: :fast | :deliberate, max_kappa: max_kappa, trigger: :retrieve_context | :analyze_topology}\n)"},{"id":"blk-69540","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100456","text":"Track:"}]},{"id":"blk-69541","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69543","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100457","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.fast_count"},{"id":"spn-100458","text":" — queries routed to fast path"}]}],"id":"blk-69542","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69545","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100459","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_count"},{"id":"spn-100460","text":" — queries routed to deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-69544","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-69547","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100461","marks":["code"],"text":"topology.route.deliberate_ratio"},{"id":"spn-100462","text":" — deliberate / total (target: < 30% on typical workloads)"}]}],"id":"blk-69546","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-69548","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-100463","text":"7.3 BendScript Performance (JavaScript — "},{"id":"spn-100464","marks":["code"],"text":"performance.now()"},{"id":"spn-100465","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-69549","kind":"code","language":"javascript","text":"const t0 = performance.now();\nconst topo = analyzeTopology(plane);\nconst elapsed = performance.now() - t0;\nconsole.debug(`[κ] topology: ${elapsed.toFixed(1)}ms, maxκ=${topo.maxKappa}, sccs=${topo.sccCount}`);"},{"id":"blk-69550","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100466","text":"Target: < 50ms at 100 nodes."}]},{"id":"blk-69551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-100467","marks":["italic"],"text":"Spec version: 0.2.0. Status: Draft (normalized). Depends on: kappa_reference.py (computation), kappa_theory_applied.md (theoretical foundations). Products affected: Graphonomous, Deliberatic, BendScript, [&] Protocol, TickTickClock, OpenSentience."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7moph55krlufvimaxilzhyrh33esihy62x3ke4qyg3drk4kkdoia","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}